  "bodyTypst": "Let $f$ be the function defined by $f(x)= e^(x) cos x$.\n\n(a) Find the average rate of change of $f$ on the interval $0 <= x <= pi$.\n\n(b) What is the slope of the line tangent to the graph of $f$ at $x = frac(3 pi,2)$ ?\n\n(c) Find the absolute minimum value of $f$ on the interval $0 <= x <= 2 pi$. Justify your answer.\n\n(d) Let $g$ be a differentiable function such that $g lr((frac(pi,2)))= 0$. The graph of $g'$, the derivative of $g$, is shown below. Find the value of $lim_(x -> pi \\/ 2) frac(f(x),g(x))$ or state that it does not exist. Justify your answer.\n\n#image(\"/imgs/ap-calc-ab-2018-frq-05-diagram-01.png\", width: 65%)",
